Use `ConfigureLifecycleEvents` in `MauiProgram.cs`:

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
#if ANDROID
    events.AddAndroid(android => android
        .OnPause(activity => { /* your background logic */ })
        .OnStop(activity => { /* fully backgrounded */ }));
#elif IOS || MACCATALYST
    events.AddiOS(ios => ios
        .DidEnterBackground(app => { /* your background logic */ }));
#endif
});
```

**Key points:**

- `OnPause` (Android) ≈ `WillResignActive` (iOS) — app lost focus but may still be visible
- `OnStop` (Android) ≈ `DidEnterBackground` (iOS) — app is fully hidden

**Cross-platform alternative:** If you don't need platform-specific APIs, use the `Window.Stopped` event instead — it maps to `OnStop` on Android and `DidEnterBackground` on iOS automatically:

```csharp
// In App.cs
protected override Window CreateWindow(IActivationState? activationState)
{
    var window = base.CreateWindow(activationState);
    window.Stopped += (s, e) => { /* runs on both platforms */ };
    return window;
}
```

⚠️ Keep handlers fast (<2s) to avoid ANR on Android or watchdog kills on iOS. Also save in `Destroying` on Android since the back button can skip `Stopped`.
